WEBVTT

00:01.680 --> 00:04.200
My first trip with Ayako-san.

00:05.190 --> 00:09.030
A lot happened, but it was fun.

00:09.520 --> 00:12.890
But the trip’s not over till we get back.

00:12.890 --> 00:18.430
I hope we can avoid any more surprises...

00:36.140 --> 00:41.260
Today I shout out another good morning courageously

00:41.260 --> 00:46.560
The sparkling chime of hope is resounding

00:47.050 --> 00:52.140
The gentle sun is always

00:52.140 --> 00:57.660
Blessing the late coming sensation of the two of them

00:57.950 --> 01:02.880
To fall in love with a goddess is the best!

01:03.090 --> 01:12.950
Even if she is a beatrice I can't control this throbbing feeling

01:12.950 --> 01:13.800
L·O·V·E

01:13.800 --> 01:15.550
I love you MA·MO·RU!

01:15.550 --> 01:17.090
These overflowing feelings

01:17.090 --> 01:19.790
Take them high into the sky

01:19.790 --> 01:24.680
Please grant me my dazzling and sparkling dream

01:24.680 --> 01:26.480
That's right MA·MO·RU!

01:26.480 --> 01:28.010
Only for you

01:28.010 --> 01:30.680
I will show you my power of miracles

01:30.680 --> 01:32.950
I will surely, surely swear

01:32.950 --> 01:38.900
I will not end my Shining Love

02:08.060 --> 02:10.560
Look at that handmade sweater.

02:10.560 --> 02:12.240
You’re grinning, Mamoru.

02:12.240 --> 02:13.240
Itsumi!

02:13.240 --> 02:14.930
I am not...

02:14.930 --> 02:17.490
OK, let’s get a commemorative photo! Pose!

02:17.490 --> 02:19.360
Hey, stop, Mitsuki!

02:20.760 --> 02:24.160
School starts tomorrow, doesn’t it?

02:24.500 --> 02:27.600
I haven’t had quite enough fun.

02:28.280 --> 02:32.840
I want one more nice event to spice it up a bit.

02:36.140 --> 02:38.740
Everyone, I’ve got an idea.

02:40.100 --> 02:42.320
There’s a place I know of nearby.

02:42.320 --> 02:44.880
I’d like to stop there.

02:44.880 --> 02:46.590
A place you know?

02:46.590 --> 02:47.690
What is it?

02:49.310 --> 02:50.390
A hot springs.

02:51.060 --> 02:52.980
A hot springs?

03:00.320 --> 03:05.330
Steam Panic

03:10.880 --> 03:13.000
Rest Area

03:23.440 --> 03:27.470
My family has always stopped here,
when returning from the villa.

03:27.470 --> 03:29.190
It’s wonderful!

03:29.190 --> 03:30.560
It’s so scenic.

03:30.560 --> 03:33.200
Yes, this is it!

03:33.200 --> 03:35.210
This is just what we needed.

03:35.210 --> 03:37.270
Sometimes, you do have good ideas.

03:37.270 --> 03:38.620
Thanks.

03:38.620 --> 03:41.280
OK, let’s allow the girls go first.

03:41.280 --> 03:43.410
Guys, lets head back to the rest area.

03:49.310 --> 03:51.250
Wow!

03:51.250 --> 03:55.450
Bath towels, soap... It’s all here!

03:55.450 --> 03:57.480
Maybe the President got them for us.

03:57.480 --> 03:58.460
I guess he did.

03:58.460 --> 04:00.730
Maya-san’s such an adult.

04:02.770 --> 04:04.260
What’s wrong?

04:04.260 --> 04:05.800
There’s no shampoo.

04:06.720 --> 04:09.250
And I was just thinking good things about him.

04:09.250 --> 04:12.480
Well, we can enjoy the hot springs.

04:12.480 --> 04:14.740
OK, let’s go.

04:14.740 --> 04:16.710
Hot springs!

04:21.950 --> 04:23.740
Rest Area

04:23.080 --> 04:24.650
Here you go, Yoshimura-sama.

04:25.680 --> 04:27.160
Thanks.

04:28.890 --> 04:31.060
This is a great place.

04:31.060 --> 04:33.620
It’s really calming.

04:33.620 --> 04:37.090
I wonder if the girls are
enjoying the onsen right now.

04:37.090 --> 04:39.310
Um, President, the hot springs here...

04:39.310 --> 04:40.740
Oh, my.

04:40.740 --> 04:43.940
I forgot something important.

04:47.030 --> 04:48.090
It’s me.

04:48.090 --> 04:49.450
Get the item we discussed in place.

04:49.450 --> 04:50.650
Hurry.

04:50.650 --> 04:51.740
That’s right.

04:58.050 --> 05:00.320
Slowly, slowly...

05:04.990 --> 05:06.920
A-A scarecrow?

05:06.920 --> 05:08.490
Shampoo.

05:11.410 --> 05:12.790
What?

05:12.790 --> 05:17.830
So my brother intends to revive that game, after all.

05:17.830 --> 05:19.670
Game?

05:19.670 --> 05:21.310
What do you mean?

05:21.310 --> 05:22.640
You can’t mean...

05:22.640 --> 05:25.510
That idiot’s planning something again?

05:26.930 --> 05:29.050
Deliver the shampoo?

05:29.050 --> 05:30.720
Yes.

05:31.100 --> 05:34.390
I forgot to give this shampoo to Shione.

05:34.390 --> 05:37.220
Mamoru-kun, I’d like you to go with me.

05:37.220 --> 05:39.170
We’re leaving it in the changing room?

05:39.170 --> 05:40.360
I don’t mind.

05:40.360 --> 05:42.360
No! We’ll present it personally!

05:44.730 --> 05:46.860
Personally...

05:47.630 --> 05:50.230
Enter the hot springs, and hand it to her.

05:55.320 --> 05:57.610
Y-You can’t mean...

05:57.610 --> 06:00.060
We’re just delivering shampoo.

06:00.060 --> 06:01.120
But wait...

06:01.120 --> 06:02.470
Why are we...

06:02.470 --> 06:06.510
When we were kids, I brought her shampoo.

06:07.740 --> 06:09.320
<i>Shione, shampoo!</i>

06:11.070 --> 06:12.190
<i>Shampoo!</i>

06:12.190 --> 06:14.790
It was so funny how she freaked out...

06:14.790 --> 06:21.040
Ever since then, every time we
come here, I bring her shampoo.

06:21.040 --> 06:23.570
When she’s in the hot springs?

06:23.570 --> 06:24.920
That’s right.

06:24.920 --> 06:28.710
Even if I take it myself... Every single year...

06:28.710 --> 06:31.570
One year, I began putting up traps to defend myself,

06:31.570 --> 06:36.950
and eventually it became a game between the two of us.

06:36.950 --> 06:41.250
But no trap ever worked
against him. Every year, I lose.

06:42.190 --> 06:45.560
Oh, how my young small chest was pained...

06:45.560 --> 06:47.590
Your chest’s still pretty small.

06:47.590 --> 06:51.080
If you don’t like it, why don’t you just avoid the hot springs?

06:52.140 --> 06:54.000
That would be retreating!

06:54.000 --> 06:56.630
My pride won’t allow it.

06:56.630 --> 07:00.790
We both grew up, and we haven’t done it for years...

07:00.790 --> 07:02.410
But I accept your challenge, Brother!

07:02.410 --> 07:04.810
W-Wait a second.

07:04.810 --> 07:08.030
That means the President’s
coming here, right?

07:08.030 --> 07:09.970
Which means...

07:09.970 --> 07:12.370
He’ll see us.

07:12.370 --> 07:13.820
You have to be kidding.

07:13.820 --> 07:15.720
Don’t get us caught up in your little squabble!

07:15.720 --> 07:17.880
Don’t worry.

07:31.370 --> 07:33.040
Cool!

07:34.460 --> 07:36.310
I thought this might happen.

07:36.310 --> 07:37.340
This is stupid.

07:37.340 --> 07:38.640
I’m going home.

07:38.640 --> 07:41.020
<i>System start!</i>

07:45.600 --> 07:47.080
Our clothes...

07:47.080 --> 07:49.200
Glad I brought my camera!

07:49.200 --> 07:51.430
Shione, what are you doing?

07:52.720 --> 07:54.600
Just a little mistake...

07:55.930 --> 07:57.330
It’s me.

07:57.330 --> 07:58.100
Yes.

07:58.100 --> 08:00.090
Seven women’s outfits to the agreed-upon place,

08:00.090 --> 08:01.000
immediately.

08:01.000 --> 08:02.710
What do we do?

08:02.210 --> 08:06.340
Yes, yes.

08:02.710 --> 08:04.150
We don’t have a choice.

08:04.150 --> 08:06.340
We have to wait till our clothes arrive.

08:07.400 --> 08:09.460
They’re on their way.

08:09.460 --> 08:10.510
Don’t worry.

08:10.510 --> 08:11.630
On their way?

08:11.630 --> 08:14.180
What if Maya-san gets here first?

08:14.180 --> 08:15.440
Don’t worry.

08:15.440 --> 08:17.650
This year, I’m going to win.

08:17.650 --> 08:19.840
You’ve never won, have you?

08:19.840 --> 08:21.750
I’m uneasy...

08:21.750 --> 08:25.660
If the stupid President comes,
I’m sending you both to hell!

08:25.660 --> 08:28.710
Are you sure?

08:28.710 --> 08:33.570
He’s got Mamoru with him.
Mamoru might come.

08:34.100 --> 08:35.670
Of course he won’t.

08:35.670 --> 08:37.970
Mamoru would never participate
in something this stupid.

08:37.970 --> 08:39.870
You can’t be sure.

08:39.870 --> 08:44.430
And if he does, will you send Mamoru to hell, too?

08:44.430 --> 08:48.720
I’m sure he wouldn’t mind being
killed by his beloved Ayako.

08:48.720 --> 08:49.670
He won’t come.

08:49.670 --> 08:51.150
He won’t!

08:51.150 --> 08:52.720
I’m not going!

08:52.720 --> 08:53.750
I’m not.

08:53.750 --> 08:56.690
Mamoru-kun, I need you to come.

08:56.690 --> 08:57.950
This year, Ayako’s there.

08:57.950 --> 08:59.440
Do you know what that means?

08:59.440 --> 09:01.030
Means?

09:01.030 --> 09:04.190
If I lose, I’m dead!

09:04.190 --> 09:05.760
This isn’t like other years.

09:05.760 --> 09:07.530
We’re risking our lives.

09:07.530 --> 09:11.220
I-I don’t think even Ayako-san...

09:12.440 --> 09:18.160
No. Even optimistically speaking, we’re toast.

09:18.160 --> 09:20.210
But I’ve got you!

09:20.210 --> 09:21.830
If you’re with me, she’ll...

09:21.830 --> 09:23.490
She’ll still be mad!

09:23.490 --> 09:25.540
Yes, but she won’t hit us as hard!

09:25.540 --> 09:28.190
It shouldn’t be too bad.

09:28.190 --> 09:33.380
Yagi-san, Kikukawa-san, say something...

09:34.300 --> 09:36.650
I will accompany you.

09:36.650 --> 09:38.550
To go!

09:38.550 --> 09:40.580
He’s not coming.

09:40.580 --> 09:42.700
He’s not!

09:42.700 --> 09:45.440
That’s right. Mamoru doesn’t have the guts.

09:46.330 --> 09:48.820
Jeez...

09:48.820 --> 09:50.010
Calm down.

09:50.010 --> 09:51.630
What’s wrong?

09:51.630 --> 09:53.210
The radar’s picking up a signal.

09:53.210 --> 09:56.510
At the villa, I put transmitters in their shoes.

09:56.510 --> 09:57.610
The number of approaching signals is...

09:58.320 --> 09:59.430
One...

09:59.430 --> 10:00.450
Two...

10:00.450 --> 10:01.160
Three...

10:01.160 --> 10:02.490
He’s not coming, he’s not coming.

10:04.180 --> 10:05.090
Four!

10:05.090 --> 10:06.260
Four?

10:06.260 --> 10:08.120
That means...

10:10.060 --> 10:11.430
Let’s go back.

10:11.430 --> 10:12.830
Seriously, let’s go back!

10:12.830 --> 10:15.740
Mamoru-kun, this is our duty as men at a hot springs.

10:15.740 --> 10:18.070
And we’ve issued the challenge.

10:18.070 --> 10:19.280
We can’t back down now.

10:19.280 --> 10:20.100
But...

10:20.100 --> 10:23.120
If we win, you can see Ayako at a hot springs.

10:24.940 --> 10:28.370
I can’t look at her like that!

10:28.370 --> 10:30.080
Man, that hurts.

10:28.370 --> 10:30.080
No! No!

10:30.080 --> 10:32.860
Yoshimura-sama is a very serious person.

10:32.860 --> 10:34.350
What about you?

10:34.350 --> 10:37.860
Won’t her grandfather be mad?

10:37.860 --> 10:42.390
Takasu-sensei would praise me
for getting one up on her.

10:42.390 --> 10:46.010
Wh-What kind of person is her grandfather

10:50.670 --> 10:51.570
Ow.

10:51.570 --> 10:53.390
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow.

10:53.390 --> 10:53.920
Yagi!

10:53.970 --> 10:55.070
Yes, boss!

11:00.250 --> 11:01.280
Splendid!

11:02.280 --> 11:03.810
W-Wow!

11:07.970 --> 11:09.990
They’ve broken through the ninth barrier!

11:09.990 --> 11:11.850
Impressive, Brother.

11:12.150 --> 11:13.730
He’s not coming. He’s not coming.

11:13.730 --> 11:15.090
Mamoru’s not coming.

11:15.090 --> 11:16.610
That’s right. He’s not.

11:17.000 --> 11:19.040
Are the clothes here yet?

11:19.040 --> 11:20.010
We’ve no choice.

11:20.010 --> 11:21.540
We’ll cooperate with Shione.

11:22.400 --> 11:24.310
This’ll be fun!

11:24.310 --> 11:25.840
What?

11:25.840 --> 11:28.640
If Shione doesn’t win, the men will come.

11:29.590 --> 11:31.220
The eighth barrier’s been broken.

11:31.220 --> 11:33.560
So has the seventh.

11:34.730 --> 11:36.750
It looks like Yagi’s helping them.

11:49.060 --> 11:52.000
I must have those beautiful guns...

11:52.000 --> 11:53.700
Yagi, no!

12:04.190 --> 12:07.100
I’ll be back!

12:07.100 --> 12:08.850
Not bad, Shione.

12:10.810 --> 12:11.550
I win!

12:11.550 --> 12:13.160
He’s not coming. He’s not coming.

12:13.160 --> 12:14.880
He’s not! He’s not!

12:14.880 --> 12:16.960
He’s not coming!

12:19.130 --> 12:21.160
The monitor’s broken.

12:21.160 --> 12:22.900
So is the radar.

12:22.900 --> 12:25.200
Looks like it was the shock of the explosion.

12:25.910 --> 12:27.160
Let me have a look.

12:27.160 --> 12:29.000
Jeez, are the clothes here yet?

12:29.000 --> 12:31.770
He’s not coming. Not coming. Not coming.

12:33.770 --> 12:35.990
<i>Where did they go?</i>

12:35.990 --> 12:37.380
<i>I’m sure they’re safe.</i>

12:37.380 --> 12:39.870
<i>I need to stop them.</i>

12:39.870 --> 12:44.340
<i>Ayako-san, I’ll... I’ll...</i>

12:49.290 --> 12:52.710
<i>Ayako-san, I’m a weak man...</i>

12:59.600 --> 13:01.430
<i>How far have I come?</i>

13:01.880 --> 13:06.010
<i>I followed Ayako-san, but I didn’t know where the villa was.</i>

13:06.010 --> 13:08.200
<i>I used up all my funds...</i>

13:08.200 --> 13:11.610
<i>But I carry my love for her in my heart.</i>

13:11.610 --> 13:14.140
<i>And as long as I do, I...</i>

13:14.140 --> 13:15.330
Ayako-san!

13:15.330 --> 13:17.080
Come back, OK?

13:20.280 --> 13:21.890
Not catching anything.

13:21.890 --> 13:24.470
Fishing is about patience, boss.

13:24.470 --> 13:25.620
Ow...

13:25.620 --> 13:27.470
What’s wrong?

13:27.470 --> 13:29.550
There were metal basins in the trees.

13:29.550 --> 13:31.190
Even pit traps!

13:31.190 --> 13:32.430
What’s going on here?

13:32.430 --> 13:34.470
Traps set by the owner, maybe.

13:34.470 --> 13:36.280
You’re getting what you deserve.

13:36.280 --> 13:38.820
You said there was a shortcut
on the mountain’s other side!

13:38.820 --> 13:40.100
It’s true!

13:40.100 --> 13:41.770
You agreed!

13:41.770 --> 13:43.040
Shut up!

13:43.040 --> 13:43.530
What?

13:43.530 --> 13:44.880
Please stop...

13:44.880 --> 13:47.720
Getting off the mountain is now our priority.

13:47.720 --> 13:50.070
We can’t be fighting.

13:50.070 --> 13:51.800
Th-That’s right.

13:51.800 --> 13:52.930
Impressive, boss.

13:52.930 --> 13:54.570
You’re smart!

13:56.200 --> 13:58.860
B-But first, I’m hungry.

13:58.860 --> 14:00.430
Let’s catch something.

14:02.270 --> 14:04.860
Mamoru’s not coming. Mamoru’s not coming.

14:05.540 --> 14:06.950
It’s not fixed yet?

14:06.950 --> 14:08.570
Hurry!

14:10.740 --> 14:12.280
It’s fixed.

14:12.280 --> 14:15.410
Someone approached one
of the automatic traps.

14:16.270 --> 14:17.580
The radar’s back?

14:21.880 --> 14:23.020
President?

14:23.020 --> 14:24.580
President!

14:25.450 --> 14:26.980
That voice...

14:29.850 --> 14:31.520
Fire!

14:35.790 --> 14:37.190
He’s persistent...

14:37.190 --> 14:38.630
Hit ’em with everything you’ve got!

14:43.900 --> 14:45.500
President!

14:47.720 --> 14:48.840
Yoshimura-sama!

14:48.840 --> 14:51.370
Hey, you’re here.

14:51.370 --> 14:54.000
No, I came to stop you.

14:54.000 --> 14:55.780
This is wrong...

14:55.780 --> 14:57.130
You’re stubborn.

14:57.130 --> 14:58.920
But so am I.

14:58.920 --> 15:00.050
President?

15:00.050 --> 15:03.660
Mamoru-kun, this is unrelated
to a desire to see girls naked.

15:03.660 --> 15:05.990
This is a matter of pride.

15:05.990 --> 15:07.800
Pride?

15:07.800 --> 15:11.630
That’s right. Others may say it’s stupid.

15:11.630 --> 15:14.120
Maybe no one will understand.

15:14.120 --> 15:15.040
But...

15:15.750 --> 15:19.580
A time comes when a man must go.

15:35.750 --> 15:37.700
<i>Go!</i>

15:40.700 --> 15:43.030
Yagi-san! Yagi-san!

15:43.910 --> 15:46.400
Watch out, Yoshimura-sama!

15:57.340 --> 15:59.070
Kikukawa-san?

15:59.070 --> 16:00.430
Why?

16:00.430 --> 16:06.450
If... If something had happened to you,
I’d never be able to face Ayako...

16:07.360 --> 16:09.970
Be happy...

16:11.820 --> 16:13.660
Kikukawa-san! Kikukawa-san!

16:16.330 --> 16:17.010
Mamoru-kun!

16:21.440 --> 16:22.290
President!

16:25.230 --> 16:27.040
Hang on, President!

16:29.920 --> 16:32.240
But... But I...

16:32.240 --> 16:34.650
You’re all that’s left...

16:34.650 --> 16:37.050
You’re the last one we can entrust...

16:37.050 --> 16:39.280
The last one who can carry our hopes...

16:49.610 --> 16:51.300
Sing a song!

16:51.810 --> 16:52.960
Stop it!

17:23.020 --> 17:26.100
<i>I’m sorry, Ayako-san! I’m sorry, Ayako-san!</i>

17:26.100 --> 17:27.980
<i>But I’m a man.</i>

17:27.980 --> 17:30.830
<i>And the time comes when a man must make a stand!</i>

17:30.830 --> 17:32.600
Signal on the radar.

17:32.600 --> 17:34.010
It’s approaching!

17:34.010 --> 17:35.800
There’s still someone moving out there?

17:35.800 --> 17:36.560
Who is it?!

17:36.560 --> 17:38.900
The President? Yagi-san? Kikukawa-san?

17:38.900 --> 17:39.640
Or...

17:41.540 --> 17:43.070
Interesting.

17:43.070 --> 17:44.410
But if he’s alone...

17:45.220 --> 17:47.240
Damn! What about the radar?

17:47.800 --> 17:49.080
It’s safe.

17:49.500 --> 17:50.750
Why?

17:50.750 --> 17:53.300
This is it, boss!

17:53.300 --> 17:56.260
These days, landowners use some serious traps.

17:56.260 --> 17:58.820
I’ve destroyed the device’s central core.

17:58.820 --> 18:00.200
Let’s go.

18:06.780 --> 18:08.600
The traps won’t work!

18:08.600 --> 18:10.610
What do we do?

18:10.610 --> 18:12.430
Don’t worry!

18:12.430 --> 18:16.040
There’s still the final barrier, the beatrice minefield.

18:16.040 --> 18:19.270
Thirty meters until he hits the minefield.

18:20.700 --> 18:22.210
Twenty-five meters.

18:22.210 --> 18:23.440
Twenty meters.

18:24.090 --> 18:25.120
Fifteen meters.

18:29.760 --> 18:33.160
Yoshimura Mamoru!

18:33.160 --> 18:34.430
Step.

18:44.470 --> 18:47.030
Haven’t the clothes arrived yet...

18:47.030 --> 18:49.060
Now, now... We won!

18:49.060 --> 18:51.620
Let’s sit back and wait.

18:51.620 --> 18:54.390
Mamoru really wasn’t there?

18:54.990 --> 18:57.850
Maybe that signal was...

18:57.850 --> 18:59.890
Th-That’s impossible.

18:59.890 --> 19:01.490
Mamoru would never...

19:09.830 --> 19:11.770
What are you doing there?

19:11.770 --> 19:15.770
M-M-Mam... Mam... Mamoru?

19:16.590 --> 19:17.870
Mamoru!

19:17.870 --> 19:18.630
Why?

19:19.000 --> 19:21.180
You survived that explosion?

19:21.180 --> 19:22.420
I believed in you.

19:22.420 --> 19:23.470
I believed in you!

19:23.470 --> 19:24.810
That’s right, Mamoru.

19:24.810 --> 19:25.790
You suck!

19:25.790 --> 19:26.490
Why?

19:26.490 --> 19:27.350
Why did you do it?

19:27.350 --> 19:28.650
Because I’m a man!

19:33.900 --> 19:35.960
Get out here, idiot President!

19:37.820 --> 19:41.390
That was splendid, Mamoru-kun.

19:41.390 --> 19:42.450
I’m a man...

19:43.260 --> 19:45.030
What did you tell him?

19:45.400 --> 19:47.870
Nothing. Not a thing.

19:47.870 --> 19:48.980
Liar!

19:48.980 --> 19:52.440
Mamoru-kun would never do
something this stupid on his own!

19:53.020 --> 19:55.460
So what is this, Shione?

19:55.460 --> 19:59.180
Naturally, I win, Brother.

19:59.180 --> 20:01.600
We changed it up a bit this year.

20:01.600 --> 20:03.850
We changed the game a little.

20:03.850 --> 20:05.550
The question now was whether Ayako

20:05.550 --> 20:09.720
would forgive Mamoru-kun when he
showed up with the shampoo.

20:09.720 --> 20:11.090
What?!

20:11.090 --> 20:13.150
I bet you would.

20:13.150 --> 20:15.070
I bet you wouldn’t.

20:15.070 --> 20:16.930
Then all of that was...

20:16.930 --> 20:18.300
A lie.

20:18.300 --> 20:21.780
Even after we were separated,
I kept an eye on Mamoru-kun, via radar.

20:21.780 --> 20:25.730
Sudou-sama explained this midway.

20:25.730 --> 20:26.870
We cooperated.

20:26.870 --> 20:28.530
All the traps were fake.

20:28.530 --> 20:30.810
They were flashy, but they lacked any real power.

20:30.810 --> 20:33.660
I got scared when the system broke.

20:33.660 --> 20:36.790
I was moved by Yoshimura-sama’s love for his friends.

20:36.790 --> 20:39.670
Miss, he’s a wonderful man!

20:39.670 --> 20:41.690
Yes, I was truly impressed!

20:42.260 --> 20:44.030
What are you talking about?

20:44.030 --> 20:45.720
I know all that, better than anyone.

20:45.720 --> 20:48.190
So, about that game.

20:48.190 --> 20:50.340
I win, of course.

20:50.340 --> 20:51.220
Yeah?

20:51.220 --> 20:52.930
She doesn’t look too mad.

20:52.930 --> 20:54.870
Oh, I am.

20:54.870 --> 20:56.730
At you!

20:57.570 --> 21:00.380
My hair! My hair!

21:03.400 --> 21:05.320
Ma’am, not there...

21:07.250 --> 21:08.930
Stupid Mamoru!

21:09.430 --> 21:11.110
I’m tired...

21:11.110 --> 21:13.090
Where are our clothes?

21:13.090 --> 21:15.450
Everyone, look here!

21:15.450 --> 21:16.760
Pose!

21:19.900 --> 21:21.670
I’m a man...

21:21.670 --> 21:23.930
I’m a man!

21:25.310 --> 21:26.970
It’s loud out there.

21:26.970 --> 21:29.110
Nice find, boss!

21:29.110 --> 21:30.940
How’s the water?

21:30.940 --> 21:32.360
Great.

21:32.360 --> 21:35.250
Why don’t you try it later?

21:38.730 --> 21:42.360
I’m a man!

22:01.290 --> 22:06.970
My heart is racing and I'm going to give you

22:06.970 --> 22:12.170
This sparkling emotion

22:12.560 --> 22:18.300
The evening color is dyed into this orange shirt

22:18.360 --> 22:23.450
I catch it from behind you and my heart throbbing

22:23.560 --> 22:30.410
It's an everyday thrill just to be with you

22:30.410 --> 22:37.840
I can't say it well enough but thank you

22:37.840 --> 22:43.040
Venus Dream the hidden power

22:43.040 --> 22:49.240
This feeling will change into that power

22:49.240 --> 22:54.360
Power Dream I found what I want to protect

22:54.360 --> 23:00.770
That is your smile and your feelings

23:15.290 --> 23:16.200
What?

23:16.200 --> 23:21.120
Why don’t I call Mamoru brother?

23:21.120 --> 23:23.990
Aw, that’s embarrassing.

23:23.990 --> 23:27.490
He’s not the type.

23:27.490 --> 23:31.650
But once in a while, he’ll really help me out when I need it.

23:31.650 --> 23:34.800
And once in a while, he’s pretty cool.

23:35.530 --> 23:38.000
Hey, you laughed, didn’t you?

23:39.400 --> 23:42.220
Next time: Together with Brother.
